  'draft', 'foundation',
  'A 4-year-old boy is referred after his GP noted hypertension at a routine visit (BP 138/88 mmHg). On examination, femoral pulses are weak and delayed compared with the brachial pulses, and blood pressure in the legs is lower than in the arms. He is otherwise well and asymptomatic. A soft systolic murmur is heard over the back.',
  'What is the most likely diagnosis?',
  array['coarctation of the aorta','radiofemoral delay','hypertension']
),
