  'draft', 'core',
  'A 3-year-old boy presents with a 2-day history of fever and a barking cough, with mild inspiratory stridor audible only when he is upset, and mild subcostal recession. He is alert, interactive, and able to drink fluids. A different 4-year-old girl presents with a 12-hour history of high fever, appears toxic and anxious, refuses to swallow (drooling saliva), sits leaning forward, and has soft inspiratory stridor with no barking cough.',
