  'draft', 'core',
  'A 6-year-old girl with known epilepsy is brought to the emergency department by ambulance mid-seizure. Paramedics report the generalised tonic-clonic seizure has now lasted 12 minutes continuously, despite one dose of buccal midazolam given by her parents 8 minutes ago at home. On arrival she remains actively seizing, and intravenous access is now secured.',
  'What is the most appropriate next step in management?',
  array['status epilepticus','seizure management','paediatric emergency']
),
