  'draft', 'foundation',
  'A 5-week-old boy is brought in with a 2-week history of vomiting after most feeds, which has become increasingly forceful and now projects across the room. He remains hungry immediately after vomiting. He is the first child of non-consanguineous parents. On examination he appears mildly dehydrated, and a firm, olive-sized mass is palpable in the right upper quadrant during a test feed. Venous blood gas shows a hypochloraemic, hypokalaemic metabolic alkalosis.',
  'What is the most appropriate initial step in management?',
  array['pyloric stenosis','metabolic alkalosis','fluid correction']
